00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:24,720
Thanks, Mignon, and thanks for the invitation. And also thanks to all of you for coming.

4
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:32,880
So, what I'm going to be doing is explaining work with David Gaiotto, where we're trying

5
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:36,960
to understand in terms of quantum field theory, a picture that's been developed in recent

6
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:43,390
work by Etingof Frenkel and Kazhdan, an analytic version of the Langlands correspondence. And

7
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:49,350
there are prior developments which they describe in their references, but I decided the only

8
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:52,950
one I would mention by name is the one I'm closest to understanding because it involves

