00:01:55,480 --> 00:02:01,110
explanation but maybe it will set the stage a little bit. So the theory apart from the

20
00:02:01,110 --> 00:02:05,750
choice of a simple E group G depends on the choice of a real coupling constant and theta angle

21
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:10,920
which combined to a complex parameter actually I left out the square root of minus one here

22
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:17,340
so that should be four pi i over e squared so tau's it parameter in the upper half plane

23
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:25,160
There's an elementary symmetry of shifting tau by one, but importantly, the theory based

24
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:29,640
on the dual group has an analogous symmetry. Well, the theory based on the dual group on

25
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:35,060
elementary grounds has an analogous parameter, tau dual, also with an elementary symmetry.

26
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:39,840
But importantly, there is something that physicists call electric magnetic duality, which goes

27
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:45,680
back to Montaigne and Olive in 1977, which says that theories based on G and G dual are

28
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:49,460
or equivalent under this mapping

29
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:52,580
where tau of the dual group is minus one over tau

30
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:54,220
times one over an integer.

31
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:56,700
The integer is one for simply-laced groups

32
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:59,480
and otherwise is two or three.

33
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:01,560
So this paper came out in 1977

