00:41:18,680 --> 00:41:24,150
on the sub-manifold L, that's Lagrangian for M-omega.

751
00:41:24,150 --> 00:41:26,230
Now, in many of the examples important

752
00:41:26,230 --> 00:41:27,550
in geometric Langlands,

753
00:41:27,550 --> 00:41:30,430
L is actually a complex Lagrangian sub-manifold,

754
00:41:30,430 --> 00:41:32,350
which means it's Lagrangian for omega,

755
00:41:32,350 --> 00:41:34,460
not just for M-omega.

756
00:41:34,460 --> 00:41:36,280
But that's a very special condition.

757
00:41:36,280 --> 00:41:38,120
Most Lagrangian A-branes don't...

758
00:41:37,700 --> 00:41:43,730
have that property. And the Geometric Langlands correspondence is formulated as a statement

759
00:41:43,730 --> 00:41:52,440
about all A-branes, not just the exceptional ones that are Lagrangian for Omega. So we could

760
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:58,040
apply the correspondence to branes that are not Lagrangian for Omega, only for M-omega.

761
00:41:59,680 --> 00:42:05,600
So here I've given an example of an important one. One of the questions was about

762
00:42:05,600 --> 00:42:09,900
but Eigenbrains, so Eigenbrains on the Judel side

763
00:42:09,900 --> 00:42:12,820
or skyscraper sheaves on the G side,

764
00:42:12,820 --> 00:42:14,220
they are Lagrangian brain supported

765
00:42:14,220 --> 00:42:16,540
on a fiber of the Hitchin vibration.

766
00:42:16,540 --> 00:42:17,820
A fiber of the Hitchin vibration

767
00:42:17,820 --> 00:42:19,700
is a complex, symplectic manifold.

768
00:42:19,700 --> 00:42:22,540
So this is an example important in geometric Langlands

769
00:42:22,540 --> 00:42:24,140
where L is complex, symplectic,

770
00:42:24,140 --> 00:42:27,980
not just symplectic for M-omega.

771
00:42:27,980 --> 00:42:29,740
But it's a highly non-generic situation.

772
00:42:29,740 --> 00:42:34,900
So Sergey and I decided to look at the opposite case

773
00:42:34,900 --> 00:42:37,480
of an A-brain that's Lagrangian for M-omega,

774
00:42:37,480 --> 00:42:41,660
but it's symplectic rather than Lagrangian for real omega.

775
00:42:41,660 --> 00:42:43,200
That's the opposite case

776
00:42:43,200 --> 00:42:45,380
from the case of a complex Lagrangian,

777
00:42:45,380 --> 00:42:49,970
complex symplectic sub-manifold.

778
00:42:49,970 --> 00:42:51,990
We showed that in this case,

779
00:42:51,990 --> 00:42:56,330
HOM from B to BCC is a quantization of L

780
00:42:56,330 --> 00:43:00,310
with symplectic structure of real omega.

781
00:43:00,310 --> 00:43:01,470
That statement only makes sense

782
00:43:01,470 --> 00:43:06,950
because L was assumed to be symplectic for real omega.

783
00:43:06,950 --> 00:43:09,310
But nevertheless, it was Lagrangian for M omega,

784
00:43:09,310 --> 00:43:10,750
so it's an A-brain.

785
00:43:10,750 --> 00:43:14,410
and we can look at HOM as an A-brain from B to BCC.

786
00:43:14,410 --> 00:43:16,310
And we showed that that vector space

787
00:43:16,310 --> 00:43:17,470
is a quantization of L

788
00:43:17,470 --> 00:43:21,040
with symplectic structure, real omega.

789
00:43:21,040 --> 00:43:25,260
That was kind of the main point of our paper.

790
00:43:25,260 --> 00:43:27,980
So for example, if Y is an affine variety,

791
00:43:27,980 --> 00:43:29,660
then the holomorphic functions in Y,

792
00:43:29,660 --> 00:43:34,340
which are deformation quantized to get HOM

793
00:43:34,340 --> 00:43:36,180
from BCC to itself,

794
00:43:36,180 --> 00:43:37,460
are analytic continuations

795
00:43:37,460 --> 00:43:40,590
of certain real analytic functions on L.

796
00:43:40,590 --> 00:43:42,150
And those real analytic functions,

797
00:43:42,150 --> 00:43:43,490
there are enough of them to be a reasonable

798
00:43:43,490 --> 00:43:45,850
quantum deformed algebra of observables.

799
00:43:45,850 --> 00:43:47,550
And those are the functions that act

800
00:43:47,550 --> 00:43:50,130
on this quantum Hilbert space.

801
00:43:50,130 --> 00:43:53,050
