854
00:46:30,490 --> 00:46:31,770
And I'll just explain heuristically

855
00:46:31,770 --> 00:46:33,850
why you should expect this criteria.

856
00:46:33,850 --> 00:46:36,370
If holomorphic functions on Y act on H,

857
00:46:36,370 --> 00:46:37,890
and H is a Hilbert space,

858
00:46:37,890 --> 00:46:39,890
one will have a notion of which holomorphic functions

859
00:46:39,890 --> 00:46:42,240
on Y are Hermitian,

860
00:46:42,240 --> 00:46:43,720
which in the classical limit ought to be

861
00:46:43,720 --> 00:46:45,660
which functions are real.

862
00:46:45,660 --> 00:46:47,660
So you should have a notion of a holomorphic function

863
00:46:47,660 --> 00:46:49,780
on Y being real.

864
00:46:49,780 --> 00:46:53,060
And that's what you have if M is a component

865
00:46:53,060 --> 00:46:54,220
of the fixed point set

866
00:46:54,220 --> 00:46:57,350
of an anti-holomorphic involution of Y.

867
00:46:57,350 --> 00:46:59,230
It gives on the holomorphic functions

868
00:46:59,230 --> 00:47:05,380
a notion of which functions on M are real.

869
00:47:05,380 --> 00:47:06,860
A holomorphic function of Y is real

870
00:47:06,860 --> 00:47:09,040
if it's real when restricted to M.

871
00:47:09,040 --> 00:47:10,700
And those are the ones that become

872
00:47:10,700 --> 00:47:13,180
Hermitian operators after quantization.

873
00:47:13,180 --> 00:47:15,820
If we don't have a condition like this on M,

874
00:47:15,820 --> 00:47:18,020
then we'd have no reasonable notion

875
00:47:18,020 --> 00:47:19,580
of what functions should become Hermitian,

876
00:47:19,580 --> 00:47:22,300
so we shouldn't expect to have a Hermitian product

877
00:47:22,300 --> 00:47:25,350
on the quantum vector space.

